    "text": "<div class=\"eng-text\"><p class=\"eng-note\">Прочитайте приведённый ниже текст. Преобразуйте слова, напечатанные заглавными буквами в конце строк, обозначенных номерами 20–28, так, чтобы они грамматически соответствовали содержанию текста. Заполните пропуски полученными словами. Каждый пропуск соответствует отдельному заданию 20–28.</p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">20</span> It was a great day yesterday. My friends and I <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> to see a performance at the Bolshoi Theatre. <span class=\"eng-word\">GO</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">21</span> You certainly know that the Bolshoi Theatre is the <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> theatre in Russia and probably in the world. <span class=\"eng-word\">FAMOUS</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">22</span> But not everyone <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> the history of the Bolshoi Theatre. <span class=\"eng-word\">KNOW</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">23</span> According to historical documents, it <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> in March 1776 when Prince Pyotr Urusov was granted Royal permission to build a public theatre in Moscow. <span class=\"eng-word\">BEGIN</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">24</span> Catherine II, Empress of Russia, was fond of arts. She <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> having a new theatre in her country. <span class=\"eng-word\">NOT MIND</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">25</span> The original building of the theatre had a hall with almost 1,000 seats, a stage and an orchestra pit. Directly over the stage there <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> boxes where the most noble fans of the theatre had their seats. <span class=\"eng-word\">BE</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">26</span> The theatre has changed several times during <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> history. <span class=\"eng-word\">IT</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">27</span> The building we can see today opened in 1825. It <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> by architect Andrei Mikhailov who was also the architect of the Maly Theatre. <span class=\"eng-word\">DESIGN</span></p><p><span class=\"eng-num\">28</span> Since that time, the building has been rebuilt and renovated several times. Now it looks beautiful from the inside and outside. If I <span class=\"eng-gap\"></span> the opportunity to go there more often, I would do it every week. <span class=\"eng-word\">HAVE</span></p></div>",
